      "code_path": "sui-move-contract/contracts/protocol/sources/entry_points/admin/emode.move::create_emode_params_inner::L161-196",
      "proof_trace": "`create_emode_params_inner` enforces `collateral_factor_bps < BPS_DENOMINATOR` (upper bound) and `create_emode_params` enforces `collateral_factor_bps < liquidation_factor_bps`, but neither checks `collateral_factor_bps > 0`. Setting `collateral_factor = 0` passes all assertions (since `0 < liquidation_factor_bps` trivially satisfies the strict `<` check), while `can_be_collateral()` checks only `liquidation_factor > 0`—so the asset is treated as valid collateral even though its health-factor weight (multiplied in market.move:1289) is zero, violating the invariant `0 < collateral_factor`.",
      "attack_scenario": "An admin calls `create_emode_params(collateral_factor_bps=0, liquidation_factor_bps=N>0, ...)` to obtain a valid `NewEMode` struct, then applies it via `update_asset_in_emode_group` or `onboard_asset_to_emode_group`; users who have deposited that asset as emode collateral see their weighted collateral value drop to zero, making their positions immediately liquidatable.",
      "checklist_id": "PROP-01b-partial1-inv-024"
    }
  ]
}

